IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-i-n1-bands`

-- LAYER-1 TESTS for the bands and limits of N 1's Schedule, in every vintage.  Expected values are hand-read from the amending notifications
-- (each rule's @ref gives the raw lines).  They say what the Schedule prints against an item number, and nothing about any person's situation.

§ `Item 11 (Remote Control Devices): the bands in each vintage`

#ASSERT `N 1 Schedule: the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n, on the date` (Date 1 1 2003) 11 EQUALS JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
#ASSERT `N 1 Schedule: the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n, on the date` (Date 31 12 2002) 11 EQUALS JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
#ASSERT `N 1 Schedule: the authorised radio frequency bands and the maximum approved field strength or power for item n, on the date` (Date 17 10 2001) 11 EQUALS JUST (LIST "26.96-27.28 MHz: 500 mW ERP", "40.66-40.70 MHz: 500 mW ERP")
